---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="A note about this kitchen">
  <section class="page-pad about-page">
    <div class="eyebrow blue">EFREN MENDOZA / AUSTIN, TEXAS</div>
    <h1>
      A collection.
      <br />A practice.
      <br />
      <i>A place at the table.</i>
    </h1>
    <div class="about-columns">
      <span class="about-mark">
        e<span>m.</span>
      </span>
      <div>
        <p class="about-intro">
          Recipes I’ve cooked, changed, found along the way, or simply want to
          make next.
        </p>
        <p>
          This kitchen moves between Mexican and Venezuelan food, a good asado,
          the weeknight chicken-and-rice rotation, and the small ritual of
          coffee.
        </p>
        <p>
          The point isn’t to get everything perfect. It’s to keep the things
          worth making again, and leave room in the margins for what changes.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/recipes/">
          Open the recipe book ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-details">
      <div>
        <span>THE EVERYDAY ROTATION</span>
        <p>Chicken, rice, something green.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>ALWAYS ROOM FOR</span>
        <p>One more person. One more cup.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>THE KITCHEN RULE</span>
        <p>No eggs. Make it your own.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="archive-note">
      <span class="eyebrow blue">ABOUT THE ARCHIVE</span>
      <p>
        Complete recipes sit alongside saved inspiration. Source notes link back
        to their original creators; kitchen drafts are proposed recipes waiting
        to be cooked and refined. Dietary labels appear only where explicitly
        recorded. The food photographs are AI-generated illustrations, not
        records of dishes cooked by Efren.
      </p>
      <p>Shopping lists and saved menus live in your browser on this device.</p>
    </section>
  </section>
</Layout>
